<h2 class=3D"wp-block-heading" id=3D"disclaimer">Disclaimer</h2>



<p class=3D"wp-block-paragraph">RPGBOT uses the color coding scheme which h=
as become common among Pathfinder build handbooks, which is simple to under=
stand and easy to read at a glance.</p>



<ul>
	<li><span class=3D"rating-red">Red</span>: Bad, useless options, or option=
s which
		are extremely situational. Nearly never useful.</li>
<li><span class=3D"rating-orange">Orange</span>: OK options, or useful opti=
ons
		that only apply in rare circumstances. Useful sometimes.</li>
<li><span class=3D"rating-green">Green</span>: Good options. Useful often.<=
/li>
<li><span class=3D"rating-blue">Blue</span>: Fantastic options, often essen=
tial
		to the function of your character. Useful very frequently.</li>
</ul><!-- Ezoic - wp_mid_content - mid_content --><div id=3D"ezoic-pub-ad-p=
laceholder-177" data-inserter-version=3D"2" data-placement-location=3D"mid_=
content"></div><!-- End Ezoic - wp_mid_content - mid_content -->



<p class=3D"wp-block-paragraph">We will not include 3rd-party content, incl=
uding content from DMs Guild, in handbooks for official content because we =
can=E2=80=99t assume that your game will allow 3rd-party content or homebre=
w. We also won=E2=80=99t cover Unearthed Arcana content because it=E2=80=99=
s not finalized, and we can=E2=80=99t guarantee that it will be available t=
o you in your games.</p>



<p class=3D"wp-block-paragraph">The advice offered below is based on the cu=
rrent <a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/2024-dnd-meta/" data-type=3D"p=
age" data-id=3D"30654">State of the 2024 DnD Character Optimization Meta</a=
> as of when the article was last updated. Keep in mind that the state of t=
he meta periodically changes as new source materials are released, and the =
article will be updated accordingly as time allows. Also be sure to check f=
or <a href=3D"https://www.dndbeyond.com/changelog#2024CoreRulesErrata" targ=
et=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener">errata</a> periodically.</p>





<h2 class=3D"wp-block-heading" id=3D"shillelagh">Rogues and Attack Spells</=
h2>



<p class=3D"wp-block-paragraph">You cannot deliver Sneak Attack with a Spel=
l Attack. This means that Cantrips
	like Fire Bolt don=E2=80=99t work, but spells which call for a Weapon Atta=
ck, like
	Booming Blade and True Strike, all work.<!-- Ezoic - wp_long_content - lon=
g_content --></p><div id=3D"ezoic-pub-ad-placeholder-178" data-inserter-ver=
sion=3D"2" data-placement-location=3D"long_content"></div><!-- End Ezoic - =
wp_long_content - long_content --><p></p>



<p class=3D"wp-block-paragraph">Gishes (characters that mix spellcasting an=
d martial capabilities) frequently
	need to choose between using attack Cantrips or using Extra Attack, and th=
e
	math there can become complicated. However, Rogues don=E2=80=99t get Extra=
 Attack.
	Unless you=E2=80=99re relying on fighting with two weapons, using a Cantri=
p is an easy
	boost to your attacks.</p>



<p class=3D"wp-block-paragraph">Because Rogue=E2=80=99s damage output comes=
 primarily from Sneak Attack, missing a
	single attack can be devastating. Rolling a second d20, either from Advant=
age
	or from a second attack roll, boosts your average damage per round (DPR) b=
y as
	much as 50%. Using a Cantrip means that you can=E2=80=99t use a Nick weapo=
n to make a
	second attack during your Attack action. Instead, consider Vex weapons lik=
e
	hand crossbows and rapiers, and use stealth or Steady Aim to get Advantage=
 on
	your first attack against a new target.</p>



