		<sup>(<a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/abbreviations/">PHB</a>)</su=
p>: Too
		situational to prepare permanently.</li>
	<li><span class=3D"rating-red">Fire Shield</span>
		<sup>(<a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/abbreviations/">PHB</a>)</su=
p>: You
		should not be drawing enough attacks to justify this.</li>
	<li><span class=3D"rating-blue">Greater Invisibility</span>
		<sup>(<a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/abbreviations/">PHB</a>)</su=
p>:
		Probably the most important spell that anyone can cast on a rogue.</li>
	<li><span class=3D"rating-orange">Hallucinatory Terrain</span>
		<sup>(<a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/abbreviations/">PHB</a>)</su=
p>: Unless
		you specifically need the 24-hour duration and the massive area of effect=
,
		Major Image will suffice.</li>
	<li><span class=3D"rating-red">Ice Storm</span>
		<sup>(<a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/abbreviations/">PHB</a>)</su=
p>:
		Terrible. Bad damage, and the difficult terrain doesn=E2=80=99t last long
		enough.</li>
	<li><span class=3D"rating-red">Leomund=E2=80=99s Secret Chest</span>
		<sup>(<a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/abbreviations/">PHB</a>)</su=
p>: Too
		situational to prepare permanently.</li>
	<li><span class=3D"rating-red">Locate Creature</span>
		<sup>(<a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/abbreviations/">PHB</a>)</su=
p>: Too
		situational to prepare permanently.</li>
	<li><span class=3D"rating-red">Mordenkainen=E2=80=99s Faithful Hound</span=
>
		<sup>(<a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/abbreviations/">PHB</a>)</su=
p>: Decent
		for defending a specific point, but not useful enough to be your only lev=
el
		4 spell each day.</li>
	<li><span class=3D"rating-red">Mordenkainen=E2=80=99s Private Sanctum</spa=
n>
		<sup>(<a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/abbreviations/">PHB</a>)</su=
p>: You get
		one level 4 spell slot every day. Do you really want to spend it on a pla=
ce
		to sleep?</li>
	<li><span class=3D"rating-blue">Otiluke=E2=80=99s Resilient Sphere</span>
		<sup>(<a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/abbreviations/">PHB</a>)</su=
p>:
		Single-target save-or-suck, and you can make it more reliable with Magica=
l
		Ambush. A good way to take a target out of a fight until you=E2=80=99re r=
eady to
		handle them.</li>
	<li><span class=3D"rating-red">Phantasmal Killer</span>
		<sup>(<a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/abbreviations/">PHB</a>)</su=
p>: If
		you=E2=80=99re going to hit a single target with a spell, you want it to =
eliminate
		or incapacitate them in one shot, and Phantasmal Killer simply doesn=E2=
=80=99t do
		that.</li>
	<li><span class=3D"rating-orange">Polymorph</span>
		<sup>(<a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/abbreviations/">PHB</a>)</su=
p>:
		Normally a fantastic combat option, but your own attacks will greatly exc=
eed
		anything that you can turn into. You might turn into something just for t=
he
		massive pool of Temporary Hit Points, but that=E2=80=99s likely not enoug=
h to
		justify your only level 4 spell slot.</li>
	<li><span class=3D"rating-red">Raulothim=E2=80=99s Psychic Lance</span>
		<sup>(<a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/abbreviations/">PHB</a>)</su=
p>: Too
		situational to prepare permanently.</li>
	<li><a class=3D"rating-blue" href=3D"https://www.dndbeyond.com/spells/1459=
7-sickening-radiance" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener">Sickening Radiance=
</a>
		<sup>(<a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/abbreviations/">XGtE</a>)</s=
up>: This
		spell is very easy to overlook. The effects are complicated, and the 4d10
		damage looks underwhelming, but don=E2=80=99t let that deter you. This is=
 a great
		spell to cast into a room then shut the door, but, even if that=E2=80=99s=
 not an
		option, it=E2=80=99s a fantastic way to handle crowds. With a 30-foot rad=
ius you can
		hit a huge number of targets, and with a 10-minute duration you can easil=
y
		kill anything stuck in the area for an extended period.
		<p>The 4d10 damage is fine, and negating invisibility is great, but the r=
eal
			appeal is the levels of Exhaustion. The penalties on d20 tests and to
			speed make it progressively easier to keep enemies in the area, and
			pushing enemies back into the area will get progressively easier the mor=
e
			times you do it. Enemies will either die from gradual damage or from
			hitting 6 levels of Exhaustion as the stacking penalties to their d20
			tests make the save functionally impossible to pass.</p>
	</li>
	<li><span class=3D"rating-orange">Spellfire Storm</span>
		<sup>(<a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/abbreviations/">FRHoF</a>)</=
sup>: The
		damage isn=E2=80=99t great and Constitution saves aren=E2=80=99t reliable=
, but the AOE is
		decently large and this can prevent enemies from casting spells. The Con
		save when casting a spell is identical to Counterspell, so you=E2=80=99re
		effectively countering every spell that enemies try to cast while in the
		area. I would only use when facing enemy spellcasters (the damage isn=E2=
=80=99t good
		enough otherwise), but with enemy spellcasters on the field this can easi=
ly
		define an encounter.
		<p>We can also compare Spellfire Storm to Moonbeam, which also creates a
			column of Radiant damage. Spellfire Storm deals the same damage as
			Moonbeam cast at the same spell level and uses the same save, but instea=
d
			of bother Shapeshifters, Spellfire Storm shuts down enemy spellcasters.
			Spellfire Storm can=E2=80=99t be moved, but the considerably larger radi=
us means
			that you don=E2=80=99t need to move it in many encounters. In close quar=
ters,
			enemies may be unable to move out of the area. Of course, that also mean=
s
			that you can=E2=80=99t use forced movement to repeatedly trigger the spe=
ll=E2=80=99s
			damage like you could with area effects which don=E2=80=99t cover the en=
tire
			battlefield.</p>
		<p><span class=3D"rating-red">Casting as a Circle Spell</span>: 25,000 gp=
 to
			do this is absolutely insane. This is something that should happen as a
			plot point, not as a player tactic. Maybe you drop this on an extraplana=
r
			gate so that your party can fight waves of demons to shut down the gate =
or
			something similarly epic and plot-defining.</p>
	</li>
	<li><span class=3D"rating-green">Spirit of Death</span>
		<sup>(<a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/abbreviations/">BoMT</a>)</s=
up>: Summon
		Undead is arguably better, but this is still a good summon.
		<p>For more help, see our
			<a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/summoning#spirit-of-death">Practi=
cal Guide to Summoning Spells</a>.</p>
	</li>
	<li><span class=3D"rating-blue">Stone Shape</span>
		<sup>(<a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/abbreviations/">PHB</a>)</su=
p>: This is
		one of the most useful spells in the game. Castles, dungeons, caves,
		mountains, and all manner of other locales include an abundance of stone.
		The ability to reshape that stone to your purposes in an instant is
		immensely useful. This is a spell limited only by your imagination. A 5-f=
oot
		cube is plenty of space to wreak all kinds of havoc if you=E2=80=99re cle=
ver.</li>
	<li><span class=3D"rating-red">Stoneskin</span>
		<sup>(<a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/abbreviations/">PHB</a>)</su=
p>: You
		have Uncanny Dodge.</li>
	<li><span class=3D"rating-orange">Storm Sphere</span>
		<sup>(<a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/abbreviations/">EEPC / XGtE<=
/a>)</sup>:
		Passable area control for an extended fight, but the damage is poor, and =
1
		minute of this probably isn=E2=80=99t enough for your single level 4 spel=
l slot.
		Sickening Radiance is much better.</li>
	<li><span class=3D"rating-blue">Summon Aberration</span>
		<sup>(<a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/abbreviations/">PHB</a>)</su=
p>: Three
		diverse and effective combat options. If you can keep the summon alive fo=
r
		the full duration, it=E2=80=99s a great way to get an ally into melee wit=
h enemies
		so that you can use Sneak Attack. Even barring that, summons are pretty
		great in combat.
		<p>For more help, see our
			<a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/summoning#summon-aberration">Prac=
tical Guide to Summoning Spells</a>.</p>
	</li>
	<li><span class=3D"rating-blue">Summon Construct</span>
		<sup>(<a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/abbreviations/">PHB</a>)</su=
p>: Not as
		effective offensively as Summon Aberration, but all three summoned
		constructs are unusually durable for creatures summoned by similar spells=
.

		<p>For more help, see our
			<a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/summoning#summon-construct">Pract=
ical Guide to Summoning Spells</a>.</p>
	</li>
	<li><span class=3D"rating-orange">Summon Elemental</span>
		<sup>(<a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/abbreviations/">PHB</a>)</su=
p>: Summon
		Aberration is better offensively, and Summon Construct provides a more
		durable summon. Summon Elemental=E2=80=99s biggest advantage is that you =
can summon
		a creature that can fight effectively underwater, but even then it=E2=80=
=99s not a
		great summon.
		<p>For more help, see our
			<a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/summoning#summon-elemental">Pract=
ical Guide to Summoning Spells</a>.</p>
	</li>
	<li><span class=3D"rating-red">Vitriolic Sphere</span>
		<sup>(<a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/abbreviations/">PHB</a>)</su=
p>:
		Bad.</li>
	<li><span class=3D"rating-green">Wall of Fire</span>
		<sup>(<a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/abbreviations/">PHB</a>)</su=
p>:
		Fantastic area control, but you get it so late that the damage isn=E2=80=
=99t great,
		and it won=E2=80=99t help you do Rogue things.</li>
	<li><span class=3D"rating-red">Watery Sphere</span>
		<sup>(<a href=3D"https://rpgbot.net/2024-dnd/abbreviations/">EEPC / XGtE<=
/a>)</sup>:
		The primary appeal here is the ability to restrain the target, then drag
		them around for the spell=E2=80=99s duration, but that consumes your Acti=
on, which
		means that you=E2=80=99re not Sneak Attacking.</li>
</ul>

